WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.378
Gentlemen if you want to sell

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:05.714
a couple hundred thousand game boys to little kids,

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.382
package it with Mario.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:12.721
But if you want to sell millions to absolutely everyone

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:13.722
around the world,

00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:17.225
package it with Tetris.

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.101
Tetris?

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:19.644
It’s the perfect game.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.147
It's an extraordinary story

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:23.648
involving lots of different factions

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:24.649
from all over the world

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.610
all pursuing this incredibly hot property.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.654
This game is poetry,

00:00:29.654 --> 00:00:32.615
art and math all working in magical synchronicity.

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:35.493
My character Henk is a publisher of games

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:38.621
who sets out on this kind of mad dash

00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:41.040
to secure the rights to Tetris.

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:41.791
Where?

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:42.584
Russia.

00:00:45.003 --> 00:00:47.213
There's this one man in the USSR

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.507
whose made this thing that everyone wants.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.843
Alexey is the designer,

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:52.719
he designed the game.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.971
Because of the laws in Russia at the time,

00:00:54.971 --> 00:00:57.140
he's denied the right to earn any money

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.684
from his game, it kind of becomes the property of the state.

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:03.146
But Henk kind of storms into his life.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.733
Henk was the first man in Russia

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.568
to whom you can talk about computers.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.069
I'm going to make you a millionaire.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.614
I do not have right to receive money from my game.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:13.865
That’s criminal. 

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:14.282
No,

00:01:14.282 --> 00:01:15.533
 

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:16.451
it is communism.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.206
Have you ever negotiated with the Soviets Mr. Rogers?

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:22.290
Do you know what it feels like to be

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.959
in a country where everyone is watching you?

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:26.419
Go home, understood?

00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:29.756
How do you get the game out of Russia

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.341
when everything's chaos there?

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.259
This is an illegal copy.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.803
He thinks I stole Tetris?

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:35.887
Affirmative.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.806
These were true visionaries that

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:40.225
broke the rules to make the world better.

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:43.770
It's an unknown story about a very well known game.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.440
Henk hits a number of walls trying to

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.026
smuggle the rights of Tetris out of the USSR

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.028
one of those blockades being the Maxwell's.

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:54.030
Kevin Maxwell, CEO of Mirrorsoft.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.156
Fantastic,

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:58.326
I would like to buy your worldwide handheld rights.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:00.119
We'll consider your offer, Mr. Rogers.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.204
I haven’t made one yet.

00:02:01.704 --> 00:02:02.204
Yes.

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:06.209
It's exciting, it's thrilling,

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:09.629
it's based on reality, it's just a lot of fun.

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:12.966
Not so often I can see the movie

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.509
when I read the screenplay but

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:15.593
this one was brilliant.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.679
Get me Tetris.

00:02:19.764 --> 00:02:22.225
It's about companionship and friendship

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.685
and that these two kindred spirits,

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:26.855
capitalists and communists have kind of come together.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:28.940
My dad put everything on the line

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.316
to chase after this game,

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.736
most people have no idea the drama the game went through

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:36.114
for it to spread to the rest of the world.

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:38.825
I think some people will feel nostalgic.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:41.703
Tetris has connection to this desire that all human beings

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.955
have to create something, to build something,

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:45.248
to put everything in order.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.126
This phrase falling blocks it's about love,

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:51.004
it doesn't matter where you're from, if you're inspired

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.256
by what you're doing there are no barriers.

00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:56.175
Tetris is a cultural zeitgeist.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.845
And it's quite exciting to think that the backstory

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.346
to this phenomenon will finally

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.806
get its moment in the sunlight.

